  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "xENbsiXElvZyn09lO7bhs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 314.41015625,
      "y": 158.00390625,
      "width": 929.1591186523438,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2086646752,
      "version": 129,
      "versionNonce": 470694880,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785960964010,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Because of the increase in the renderer complexity and size, I had to refactor a lot of things.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Because of the increase in the renderer complexity and size, I had to refactor a lot of things.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "BLAKqB5P44h83qOEznZyO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 338.7837219238281,
      "y": 231.21484375,
      "width": 1072.6190185546875,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1961749024,
      "version": 622,
      "versionNonce": 687471584,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785961063253,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Previously, I described flat shading, gouraud shading and phong shading. However, I didn't specify where\nthey were allocated.\n\nAt the start, everywhing was in the rasterizer method. However, I needed to add more options and, for that,\nI found myself in the obligation to the separate every phase in the graphics pipeline.\n\nThe result? Everything broke...",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Previously, I described flat shading, gouraud shading and phong shading. However, I didn't specify where\nthey were allocated.\n\nAt the start, everywhing was in the rasterizer method. However, I needed to add more options and, for that,\nI found myself in the obligation to the separate every phase in the graphics pipeline.\n\nThe result? Everything broke...",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WQtJ6T6eZ5EPHH9JmKe8b",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 292.28125,
      "y": 482.359375,
      "width": 955.63916015625,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 244197920,
      "version": 10,
      "versionNonce": 2101982176,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785961092814,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Flat, Gouraud, and Phong are indeed three ways of solving the same problem: approximating how a\nsurface reflects light. They are lighting models (or, more precisely, shading techniques).\n\nThe main difference between them is where the lighting is evaluated.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Flat, Gouraud, and Phong are indeed three ways of solving the same problem: approximating how a\nsurface reflects light. They are lighting models (or, more precisely, shading techniques).\n\nThe main difference between them is where the lighting is evaluated.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "JQ_h_D-BKY-omFZ7hWGKm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 336.6480000091783,
      "y": 1507.1602968852612,
      "width": 535.3595581054688,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 559761376,
      "version": 249,
      "versionNonce": 681051104,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785961539611,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The flat shading is evaluated ONCE PER PRIMITIVE.\nIt doens't interpolate anything.\nIts implementation in GLSL would look like this:",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The flat shading is evaluated ONCE PER PRIMITIVE.\nIt doens't interpolate anything.\nIts implementation in GLSL would look like this:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "8P4lszXsUI4FtASQNlqem",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 458.85268905946214,
      "y": 1602.2297251845896,
      "width": 241.99966430664062,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1736609760,
      "version": 92,
      "versionNonce": 1209799200,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785961387541,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "flat out vec3 normal;\n\nv0.normal = faceNormal\nv1.normal = faceNormal\nv2.normal = faceNormal",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "flat out vec3 normal;\n\nv0.normal = faceNormal\nv1.normal = faceNormal\nv2.normal = faceNormal",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xLEsmN6nrFR6ICTVtUYnn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 243.90225219726562,
      "y": 688.8828125,
      "width": 709.4793701171875,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1429373472,
      "version": 395,
      "versionNonce": 1637708320,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785961445238,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Phong shading is evaluated ONCE PER FRAGMENT.\nSo it's expected to find its implementation in the fragment shader\nand it interpolates the normal. Because of being evaluated per fragment,\nit's so precise.\nIts implementation in GLSL would look like this:",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The Phong shading is evaluated ONCE PER FRAGMENT.\nSo it's expected to find its implementation in the fragment shader\nand it interpolates the normal. Because of being evaluated per fragment,\nit's so precise.\nIts implementation in GLSL would look like this:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "H7Bj4Uv6sXOp0-sveBq1o",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 356.16796875,
      "y": 615.109375,
      "width": 912.5391235351562,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 948991968,
      "version": 201,
      "versionNonce": 1528336928,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785961266820,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Illumination models / shadings are not programmed all in the fragment shader,\nbut sometimes they need things in the vertex shader or in the rasterizer or geometry shader",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Illumination models / shadings are not programmed all in the fragment shader,\nbut sometimes they need things in the vertex shader or in the rasterizer or geometry shader",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TmoymGyna0rH6aS2QPGIB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 224.51953125,
      "y": 826.7421875,
      "width": 428.9993896484375,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1824660448,
      "version": 27,
      "versionNonce": 278828000,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785961344022,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "out vec3 normal;\n\nvoid main()\n{\n    normal = vertexNormal;\n    gl_Position = MVP * vertexPosition;\n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "out vec3 normal;\n\nvoid main()\n{\n    normal = vertexNormal;\n    gl_Position = MVP * vertexPosition;\n}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "x2Q2jrb8S44NCh-uC3s2E",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 764.8828125,
      "y": 821.3046875,
      "width": 549.999267578125,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1107628576,
      "version": 21,
      "versionNonce": 1913713632,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785961352207,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "in vec3 normal;\n\nvoid main()\n{\n    float intensity = dot(normal, lightDirection);\n    color = diffuseColor * intensity;\n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "in vec3 normal;\n\nvoid main()\n{\n    float intensity = dot(normal, lightDirection);\n    color = diffuseColor * intensity;\n}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
